  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> is very small as compared to the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>, so that the cube and other higher powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mi>a</mi></mfrac></math> can be neglected in the identity<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math> is :</p>",
